-- Records which book was read most recently, so the library can be ordered by it.
--
-- A counter rather than a clock, exactly as `translation_cache.usedAt` is: it is
-- one past the highest in the table, stamped whenever a position is written.
-- That answers "which book did I read last" without trusting a device clock that
-- can be changed or can go backwards.
--
-- Every position stored before this version takes 0, which puts those books
-- behind every book read since, in no particular order among themselves. There
-- is nothing more honest available - what was never recorded cannot be
-- recovered - and the order corrects itself as books are opened again.
ALTER TABLE reading_position ADD COLUMN readAt INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
